{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"87eae90fb7cd26a5ddbf29f2e75d5bf43a69606e319c8baef047d6cee03704b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"observability.sh metric publishing","key_entities":["infra/scripts/observability.sh","aws cloudwatch put-metric-data","offset file","replication","voter","merge-change","deploy","G2P","shared deferral/interrupt helper","tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py"],"problem_keywords":["cumulative counter","offset acknowledgement","cloudwatch","metric loss","transient failure","observability"],"propositions":["Cumulative counter metric offsets are persisted before CloudWatch put-metric-data completes, causing transient publish failures to permanently lose the failed interval's delta count.","Seven metric streams across six code shapes (replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, shared helpers, G2P) share the same defect pattern of premature offset acknowledgement.","Reordering offset advancement to occur only after successful AWS publication prevents data loss while preserving systemd exit-zero behavior and error handling semantics.","A whole-script PATH-shim regression test parameterizes all affected streams to prove offsets remain byte-identical after forced failures and accumulated deltas republish on retry."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787798900048737001,"uuid":"78f59f4a-f7ef-42c7-bc42-f4ff5b76da9e"}